// C++ Helper Function for Forward List Manipulation

#include <forward_list>
#include <string>

void insertAfterFirstOccurrence(std::forward_list<std::string>& list, const std::string& firstString, const std::string& secondString) {
    auto it = list.before_begin();

    for (auto nextIt = list.begin(); nextIt != list.end(); ++nextIt) {
        if (*nextIt == firstString) {
            list.insert_after(nextIt, secondString);
            return;
        }
        it = nextIt;
    }

    // If the first string is not found, append to end
    list.insert_after(it, secondString);
}
```

In this implementation:
- The AngularJS controller function `refreshDialogFields` handles multiple dialog fields and their dynamic refresh based on server responses. It uses `$http.get` to make asynchronous requests for data.
- The C++ helper function `insertAfterFirstOccurrence` efficiently manages a forward list by inserting after the first occurrence of a specified string, or appending if not found. This can be used to maintain metadata related to the updates in dialog fields."]

